«ночь.log» — a film in the CRT ASCII Terminal style (Lemo-Opuscar library).

IMAGES, FOOTAGE, MODELS
- None. Every character, the picture made of letters, the screen glass and glow are drawn in code (term.js, main.js, crt.js).
  No photographs, no AI-generated images.

FONT (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
- IBM Plex Mono Medium — IBM — https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/ibmplexmono (fonts/IBMPlexMono-OFL.txt)

VOICE
- Russian narration: Gemini text-to-speech (model gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts, voice "Puck") through the Gemini API
  (Google AI Studio), tools/tts_gemini.py, with the film owner's API key. Synthetic voice, not a recording of a person.
  Check Google's Gemini API terms for how generated audio may be used.
- Earlier draft voice (tools/tts_ru.py): RHVoice "Pavel", pitched up; not used in the final film.

MUSIC
- Original analogue-synth score synthesised in code (music/score.py); no samples.

SOUND EFFECTS
- Keys, teletype ticks, relay, degauss, error beeps, bell, particle ticks, fan and hum: synthesised in mix.py.

CODE
- term.js, crt.js, mix.py and the synth kernels in music/score.py are adapted from the Lemo-Opuscar library's
  styles/ascii-crt/demo (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Lemomo (LemoLab); text in LICENSE-MIT.txt).
